4. EVENT CLASSIFICATION

All incoming mutations are classified:

4.1 Event Types

Type	Meaning

PROPOSE	suggested change
CONFIRM	validated change
REJECT	invalid mutation
MERGE	combined change set
DEFER	delayed execution



---

5. CONSENSUS PIPELINE

1. ingest events (multi-agent stream)
2. normalize structure (GNPL schema validation)
3. detect conflicts (node/edge overlap)
4. score proposals (multi-factor evaluation)
5. resolve state
6. emit canonical event stream


---

6. SCORING MODEL

Each event gets a Consensus Score (CS):

CS = (alignment × 0.35)
   + (consistency × 0.25)
   + (redundancy_penalty × -0.20)
   + (system_impact × 0.20)


---

Scoring Dimensions

Metric	Meaning

alignment	matches JARVIS intent
consistency	matches existing graph structure
redundancy_penalty	overlap detection (NEMESIS)
system_impact	global effect magnitude



---

7. CONFLICT RESOLUTION RULES

7.1 NODE CONFLICT

If same node modified by multiple agents:

Priority order:

AEGIS validation > HALO integrity > highest CS score > latest timestamp


---

7.2 EDGE CONFLICT

If relationships diverge:

Resolution modes:

Mode	Behavior

MERGE	combine weights
SPLIT	create parallel edges
PRUNE	remove weakest
RECLASSIFY	change edge type



---

7.3 STATE CONFLICT

If Supabase ≠ GitHub ≠ GRID:

HUGINN reconciliation trigger
→ generate canonical snapshot
→ overwrite runtime state


